<title>SRI LANKA: Kelani dips 10 pct on retail sales.</title>
<headline>Kelani dips 10 pct on retail sales.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Kelani Tyres Ltd fell 10 percent, or 75 cents, to 6.75 rupees as retail investors sold the stock in early Friday trade, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Small investors are getting out with substantial capital gains, which have accrued to them in under one month,&quot; said a broker who declined to be identified.</p>
<p>Colombo stocks have risen substantially in the past month on improved investor sentiment.</p>
<p>Kelani Tyres is Sri Lanka's main manufacturer of rubber tyres and tubes.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
